WEBVTT

00:04.430 --> 00:05.480
<i>Senpai?</i>

00:06.420 --> 00:09.480
<i>She doesn't stay late enough 
to eat dinner in the office often...</i>

00:09.650 --> 00:12.140
March on, Meowtaro!

00:12.140 --> 00:16.060
Meow, meow, meow! Meow, meow, meow!

00:13.500 --> 00:15.320
<i>She's singing her heart out!</i>

00:16.670 --> 00:17.580
<i>She noticed me?</i>

00:19.830 --> 00:22.420
March on, Meowtaro!

00:21.150 --> 00:23.050
<i>She kept singing?!</i>

00:22.420 --> 00:24.370
Meow, meow, meow!

00:24.780 --> 00:27.000
<i>And she wants me to join in?!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:29.000
Meow, meow, meow!

00:29.550 --> 00:32.510
Good job, Shinozaki-san! 
That was nicely done.

00:33.820 --> 00:36.060
<i>What a cute abuse of authority.</i>

00:37.440 --> 00:44.120
<i>Oh, I love you so much, I just have to laugh</i>

00:48.980 --> 00:53.740
My Tiny Senpai

00:54.490 --> 00:56.820
<i>We've got an emergency here</i>

00:57.240 --> 00:59.600
<i>Are you paying attention, me?</i>

00:59.990 --> 01:05.830
<i>There's someone other than me 
dancing around inside of my heart</i>

01:05.830 --> 01:08.080
<i>I want to talk to her</i>

01:08.580 --> 01:11.130
<i>I want to touch her</i>

01:11.130 --> 01:16.620
<i>Look, I get it, but for now try to pipe down</i>

01:17.130 --> 01:19.840
<i>What in the world am I doing?</i>

01:19.840 --> 01:22.600
<i>You're right next to me</i>

01:22.600 --> 01:28.850
<i>And this is the perfect chance...</i>

01:29.600 --> 01:30.430
<i>HONEY</i>

01:30.430 --> 01:35.140
<i>I'm trapped by that sweet rich taste</i>

01:35.140 --> 01:38.350
<i>And I don't think I can ever escape</i>

01:38.350 --> 01:40.850
<i>I may as well just sink into it</i>

01:40.850 --> 01:41.680
<i>HONEY</i>

01:41.680 --> 01:46.450
<i>It's another day in your dazzling presence</i>

01:46.670 --> 01:49.460
<i>We may never be 
on the same page with this love but</i>

01:49.460 --> 01:55.890
<i>Oh, I love you so much, I just have to laugh</i>

02:09.480 --> 02:13.480
#11 Can I Give You a Big Hug?

02:10.980 --> 02:13.090
What should I drink?

02:15.020 --> 02:17.990
Working late on your entry? Good for you.

02:18.340 --> 02:20.480
Here, for you.

02:20.480 --> 02:22.120
Thank... you...

02:22.690 --> 02:25.620
Why not just throw together something simple?

02:25.970 --> 02:29.700
Well, I'm headed home. See you around!

02:31.930 --> 02:34.260
Can't just... throw something together.

02:34.740 --> 02:36.530
Need to help the director aim higher...

02:38.960 --> 02:40.970
Good morning.

02:42.850 --> 02:44.890
What's wrong, everyone?

02:44.890 --> 02:47.140
I should be the one asking you that!

02:47.440 --> 02:51.150
<i>The deadline for the competition 
is soon. He might be overdoing it...</i>

02:51.310 --> 02:54.250
Oh, I'm totally fine!

02:54.250 --> 02:56.170
<i>Is what I say but...</i>

02:56.780 --> 02:59.860
<i>I'm freaking out on the inside!</i>

03:00.220 --> 03:03.620
<i>The pressure of competing directly 
with someone at work for the first time,</i>

03:03.620 --> 03:06.990
<i>the responsibility of needing 
to keep our manager with us...</i>

03:06.990 --> 03:13.130
<i>It's so much I could use some rehab, 
but I can't tell Senpai that!</i>

03:13.450 --> 03:16.800
See...? I'm fine... 
Now, let's get to work...

03:20.530 --> 03:21.930
Shinozaki-san.

03:24.010 --> 03:26.660
Specially made by your senpai, 
it's the kanji for "person."

03:26.660 --> 03:28.520
Please, eat up.

03:30.430 --> 03:32.360
Wh-Why?

03:32.360 --> 03:35.980
You're worried about your proposal for 
the competition being perfect, aren't you?

03:36.790 --> 03:41.070
Please don't be afraid to fail. 
It doesn't matter if it goes smoothly.

03:41.670 --> 03:44.570
I'd even say this contest is about 
accepting that kind of thing.

03:44.970 --> 03:47.340
Just swing as hard as you can!

03:47.340 --> 03:49.450
And it's just accepted I'll miss?

03:50.410 --> 03:51.460
Thank you.

03:51.460 --> 03:51.960
Yep!

03:51.960 --> 03:54.210
<b>Product Development</b>

03:51.960 --> 03:54.210
<b>Group 1</b>

03:52.890 --> 03:54.210
Magnificent!

03:54.590 --> 03:58.480
The concept, the targeting... 
Both are clearly laid out and easy to grasp.

03:58.480 --> 03:59.970
Thank you.

03:59.970 --> 04:03.730
All you need now is an image to 
illustrate the complete project

04:00.460 --> 04:03.220
<b>The Ultimate Meowtaro</b>

04:03.730 --> 04:06.180
and it'll be an even easier sell.

04:06.180 --> 04:07.740
An illustration...

04:07.740 --> 04:10.720
Yeah. Even a simple one would be fine.

04:12.290 --> 04:16.110
You're almost there. 
Don't worry, Kurusu. You can do this!

04:18.380 --> 04:19.510
Right...

04:24.250 --> 04:26.780
<i>Senpai helped me calm down some.</i>

04:27.240 --> 04:29.290
<i>Okay, let's do this...</i>

04:30.090 --> 04:31.080
Oh, sorry!

04:45.050 --> 04:46.760
Hey, Senpai...

04:48.090 --> 04:51.540
You know that girl, Kurusu, 
in Development Group 1?

04:51.540 --> 04:53.520
Sure, I do.

04:53.520 --> 04:56.820
She's taking on the new hire contest like me,

04:56.820 --> 05:00.660
and I think she's feeling 
just as much pressure.

05:02.010 --> 05:06.160
If you see her, I'd appreciate it if you 
could try and help her feel better...

05:08.370 --> 05:11.330
Sorry, I know I shouldn't be 
asking you to do this!

05:11.330 --> 05:14.000
But I think she'd be too on-guard around me.

05:14.370 --> 05:18.000
Not to mention, I may be being 
nosy for no good reason.

05:20.050 --> 05:21.250
Understood.

05:21.560 --> 05:23.930
I'll keep that in mind.

05:23.930 --> 05:25.260
I appreciate it.

05:33.390 --> 05:34.560
Still working?

05:37.530 --> 05:40.520
You're from Development Group 2...

05:40.980 --> 05:42.450
I'm Katase Shiori.

05:42.920 --> 05:45.030
Do you always stay this late?

05:46.210 --> 05:47.850
That's none of your business.

05:48.340 --> 05:51.910
There are some things a third party 
might have a clearer view on, though.

05:52.330 --> 05:54.410
Group 2 is the enemy.

05:54.410 --> 05:56.290
I have nothing to say to you.

05:56.290 --> 05:58.250
Do you mind if I sit with you?

05:58.250 --> 05:59.430
Listen to me!

06:00.460 --> 06:02.040
That pouch...

06:02.590 --> 06:05.800
It was released for Meowtaro's 
20th anniversary, wasn't it?

06:06.470 --> 06:07.930
You recognize it?!

06:07.930 --> 06:10.110
I have one, too.

06:10.740 --> 06:13.530
There was another one 
that came out with a ribbon...

06:13.530 --> 06:16.140
I have that one, too!

06:16.140 --> 06:20.370
Meowtaro's head was rounder 
back then, with smaller eyes,

06:20.370 --> 06:23.540
and you could tell the art was more 
analog, but that made it cuter...

06:24.690 --> 06:26.940
A-And well...

06:26.940 --> 06:32.450
Even though this is the Meowtaro company... 
I don't get many chances to talk about him...

06:35.090 --> 06:37.210
Please, have a seat.

06:37.210 --> 06:38.960
Thank you.

06:40.340 --> 06:42.740
If you like Meowtaro that much,

06:42.740 --> 06:45.500
you must be really motivated 
for the rookie competition, too.

06:49.940 --> 06:51.350
Katase-san...

06:52.820 --> 06:57.720
Katase-san, is there anything 
you have trouble with at work?

07:01.150 --> 07:03.190
A whole lot of things!

07:03.190 --> 07:06.320
Laying out diagrams and adjusting text...

07:11.220 --> 07:13.310
Could you look at this?

07:16.630 --> 07:18.880
Does it remind you of any Taro in particular?

07:18.880 --> 07:21.080
That's a very leading question!

07:21.900 --> 07:24.840
I'm no good at art...

07:25.500 --> 07:27.530
I've managed to keep that 
a secret the past year.

07:28.180 --> 07:30.290
But I can't anymore...

07:32.540 --> 07:35.720
I don't want to disappoint her.

07:36.410 --> 07:39.460
I've tried so many times...

07:40.030 --> 07:41.230
but I just can't get better.

07:43.670 --> 07:47.110
I want to do a good job, Katase-san!

07:47.750 --> 07:50.110
How can I deliver for her?

07:50.110 --> 07:52.610
What do I do?

07:54.230 --> 07:55.620
Maybe you should just...

07:55.970 --> 07:58.370
tell her that you can't do it.

08:00.060 --> 08:01.920
But if I do that...

08:01.920 --> 08:05.100
Admitting when you can't do 
something is part of your job.

08:07.950 --> 08:09.140
Besides...

08:11.010 --> 08:15.270
No one's going to ridicule you
for having tried your best.

08:19.130 --> 08:22.220
Okay... I'll try and tell her.

08:25.110 --> 08:25.990
Director.

08:27.750 --> 08:30.490
I've... updated my proposal.

08:31.570 --> 08:32.900
Please, look...

08:33.220 --> 08:37.810
Sure. Knowing you, Kurusu, 
I'm sure it's evolved a fair...

08:39.160 --> 08:44.160
<b>The Ultimate Meowtaro</b>

08:40.170 --> 08:41.740
This art...

08:41.740 --> 08:43.750
I'm... so sorry.

08:44.480 --> 08:49.660
I tried, but... it was... 
the best I could do...

08:50.590 --> 08:57.180
You said I would be able 
to do it... but I failed!

09:01.580 --> 09:02.930
No, you didn't...

09:03.340 --> 09:05.190
You didn't fail, Kurusu.

09:05.620 --> 09:07.370
I should be the one to apologize.

09:07.970 --> 09:11.440
I thought I was encouraging you, 
but I was just pouring on more pressure.

09:12.150 --> 09:13.770
Please, forgive me, Kurusu.

09:14.460 --> 09:15.690
Director...

09:17.460 --> 09:21.050
Hanaoka-san, could you help 
with Kurusu's proposal?

09:21.050 --> 09:22.200
Sure.

09:22.530 --> 09:23.650
Sorry about this...

09:23.650 --> 09:25.210
It's no problem at all.

09:25.850 --> 09:28.360
There's a couple of days left 
before the deadline!

09:28.360 --> 09:31.460
We're going to support Kurusu 
as much as we can in that time!

09:31.460 --> 09:33.460
Yeah!

09:33.930 --> 09:37.100
Development Group 1 is really motivated.

09:37.100 --> 09:37.720
Yeah.

09:41.760 --> 09:43.050
<i>What a relief...</i>

09:46.230 --> 09:50.980
He's under a lot of pressure himself, but he's 
still nice enough to worry about others...

09:55.660 --> 09:58.130
Did I do something funny?

09:58.130 --> 10:01.550
Not at all. I'm just impressed 
with you, Shinozaki-san.

10:02.580 --> 10:05.110
Wh-What for, Senpai?

10:06.000 --> 10:08.370
March on, Meowtaro!

10:08.370 --> 10:09.980
Meow, meow, meow!

10:09.980 --> 10:12.000
Meow, meow, meow!

10:12.460 --> 10:16.290
<i>My Tiny Meowtaro</i>.

10:16.290 --> 10:17.580
You sure that's the title?

10:18.830 --> 10:20.890
It's finally the day of the competition.

10:21.140 --> 10:23.640
Everything ready, Shinozaki-san?

10:23.970 --> 10:25.640
Yep! All set.

10:26.070 --> 10:28.140
You're absolutely sure you're ready?

10:28.140 --> 10:30.400
I am really sure that I'm all set!

10:32.390 --> 10:33.900
I have to say...

10:34.180 --> 10:36.900
I didn't expect you to make 
a Meowtaro costume...

10:37.260 --> 10:39.220
Are you a goddess, Hayakawa-san?!

10:39.220 --> 10:40.930
Not really, no.

10:40.930 --> 10:45.070
Compared to my usual, cosplay it was 
pretty simple, so it's not like...

10:43.810 --> 10:45.070
Your usual what?

10:45.580 --> 10:48.700
Uh, er, nothing! Never mind!

10:49.100 --> 10:50.040
Oh, my.

10:50.510 --> 10:54.220
Thank you for all your help, Senpai.

10:54.220 --> 10:55.330
It's all right.

10:56.650 --> 11:00.350
Senpai, is it just me, or are you 
more nervous than I am?

11:00.780 --> 11:03.940
My direct subordinate is entering his 
biggest moment of the entire year!

11:03.940 --> 11:06.430
Of course I am!

11:07.580 --> 11:09.430
I am so full of butterflies right now...

11:09.430 --> 11:12.880
Senpai, calm down. It'll be okay.

11:09.430 --> 11:12.880
Is there anything else I can do?

11:14.920 --> 11:16.100
Kurusu-san.

11:17.130 --> 11:22.320
During the presentations... I go on before you.

11:22.320 --> 11:26.200
Hrmmm

11:22.780 --> 11:26.200
It kind of ended up feeling like 
a showdown, didn't it?

11:26.820 --> 11:28.970
Let's both do our best.

11:28.970 --> 11:29.810
Um...

11:31.300 --> 11:32.170
Thank you.

11:34.380 --> 11:38.800
Katase-san mentioned... 
you were worried about me.

11:41.350 --> 11:44.930
I'm... grateful.

11:46.780 --> 11:47.680
Sure.

11:48.350 --> 11:49.210
But...

11:50.110 --> 11:54.810
We're going to win. 
Win, and take your manager.

11:55.630 --> 11:58.020
I don't intend on losing, either.

11:58.020 --> 12:00.570
We're going to win, and keep our manager!

12:04.570 --> 12:07.020
Looking forward to your presentation.

12:08.950 --> 12:11.300
Okay! Let's do this!

12:12.710 --> 12:15.980
This talk about losing 
or keeping the manager...

12:15.980 --> 12:18.120
What's that all about?

12:19.100 --> 12:22.420
Uh, well... the truth is...

12:22.970 --> 12:24.550
The truth is...?

12:27.430 --> 12:28.930
Excuse me?!

12:31.480 --> 12:34.490
Report! Stay in contact! Consult!

12:31.930 --> 12:38.190
<b>Report</b>

12:32.810 --> 12:38.190
<b>Stay in contact</b>

12:33.690 --> 12:38.190
<b>Consult</b>

12:34.490 --> 12:36.880
You didn't do any one of those!

12:36.880 --> 12:38.190
Sorry...

12:38.500 --> 12:40.300
I knew about it.

12:40.300 --> 12:41.120
Me, too.

12:41.120 --> 12:43.110
So I'm the only one who didn't?!

12:44.410 --> 12:46.580
Maybe we can still negotiate...

12:46.580 --> 12:50.280
But she's probably already into her proposal...

12:50.280 --> 12:52.250
What do we do?!

12:52.790 --> 12:53.750
Senpai.

12:55.770 --> 12:58.130
Specially made by your kouhai, 
it's the kanji for "person."

12:59.860 --> 13:03.260
I really am sorry that 
I didn't tell you sooner.

13:03.780 --> 13:08.260
But I've been under your guidance 
for a whole year now.

13:12.210 --> 13:13.770
I know I won't lose.

13:18.690 --> 13:21.580
Gosh... if you put it like that...

13:23.020 --> 13:25.280
I won't be able to say anything back.

13:28.810 --> 13:32.040
Shinozaki-san is guaranteed to win 
the most valuable rookie award!

13:32.040 --> 13:32.780
Right!

13:32.780 --> 13:35.790
You just need spirit! Let's all huddle up!

13:35.790 --> 13:36.900
Okay!

13:35.790 --> 13:36.900
Okay...

13:36.900 --> 13:39.420
Development Group 2, fight!

13:39.420 --> 13:41.270
Yeah!

13:41.920 --> 13:43.920
Group 1

13:41.920 --> 13:43.920
Team Kurusu

13:42.540 --> 13:46.180
That was the presentation from 
Kurusu's team with Development Group 1.

13:53.380 --> 13:57.940
Next will be Shinozaki's team 
from Development Group 2.

14:00.190 --> 14:04.500
<i>I know I said he was guaranteed 
to win most valuable rookie...</i>

14:04.500 --> 14:05.940
<i>but I'm still worried.</i>

14:06.970 --> 14:12.450
Our proposal involves coming up 
with new ways to share "fun."

14:12.930 --> 14:17.110
"Taking what I enjoy today, and letting 
other people enjoy it tomorrow."

14:17.620 --> 14:19.830
And in order to make that possible...

14:20.540 --> 14:23.800
<b>Group 2</b>

14:20.540 --> 14:23.800
<b>Team Shinozaki</b>

14:21.010 --> 14:23.800
we will need Meowtaro, the super friend!

14:24.180 --> 14:25.730
Super friend?

14:26.630 --> 14:28.300
Friends...

14:29.660 --> 14:31.850
Friends, huh?

14:30.800 --> 14:36.180
Strategy meeting
Friends

14:31.850 --> 14:32.750
Yes.

14:33.540 --> 14:36.180
It's something that came to mind 
when we were with the preschool class.

14:37.090 --> 14:39.640
There're unlimited ways to have fun...

14:39.640 --> 14:43.570
What if there was someone who existed 
to help people share that fun?

14:43.940 --> 14:45.820
What if they had that kind of friend?

14:46.120 --> 14:47.150
I see...

14:47.700 --> 14:52.070
I was hoping to ask you all about 
what you heard about from the kids.

14:52.680 --> 14:55.240
There was one who liked skateboarding.

14:55.240 --> 14:57.540
I remember one who was good with magic tricks.

14:57.540 --> 14:58.770
Nice!

14:59.070 --> 15:03.500
This friend could recommend 
those kinds of things,

15:03.500 --> 15:06.460
and it'll create fondness and 
identification almost instantly!

15:06.460 --> 15:07.600
Wow!

15:07.600 --> 15:09.400
Look at him go on that skateboard.

15:09.400 --> 15:10.970
I wanna try that.

15:10.970 --> 15:12.690
Looks like fun!

15:13.110 --> 15:15.720
<i>Things are working out 
just like Shinozaki-san planned.</i>

15:15.720 --> 15:18.570
Is that Shinozaki-kun inside the suit?

15:18.570 --> 15:20.480
Oh, no! I think I might fall for him!

15:21.870 --> 15:26.480
<i>It's working out as planned, 
but maybe he's overdoing it.</i>

15:27.020 --> 15:32.240
<i>Besides, Meowtaro is Meowtaro. There's not 
supposed to be anyone "in the suit."</i>

15:37.610 --> 15:38.770
Wow!

15:38.770 --> 15:39.760
Cute!

15:39.760 --> 15:41.250
That was amazing!

15:41.250 --> 15:42.820
You're amazing, Meowtaro.

15:42.100 --> 15:46.130
<i>Aren't they all getting a little 
touchy with that costume?</i>

15:42.820 --> 15:44.030
So cute!

15:46.380 --> 15:50.800
<i>You're grown adults. You should realize 
there's someone inside that suit!</i>

15:50.800 --> 15:52.510
<b>Completely ignoring what she
was thinking minutes ago</b>

15:53.710 --> 15:54.890
<i>But...</i>

15:55.580 --> 16:00.510
<i>That was a wonderful finish 
for your first year.</i>

16:02.050 --> 16:05.020
That was Team Shinozaki from Development Group 2.

16:08.020 --> 16:09.780
Good work.

16:10.140 --> 16:12.450
Your presentation was amazing!

16:12.870 --> 16:15.740
I'm sure you'll win 
the most valuable rookie award!

16:17.250 --> 16:20.590
It looks like Hayakawa-san 
went back to her seat already.

16:21.290 --> 16:26.290
And, well... I know you might be 
feeling tired right now, but...

16:27.460 --> 16:29.670
I was hoping I could ask for something.

16:30.670 --> 16:35.390
Can I give you a big hug, too?

16:37.610 --> 16:41.430
I-It's just that everyone else was doing it, 
and I was wondering what it was like!

16:43.610 --> 16:48.620
Why are you running?! 
You let everyone else touch you lots!

16:48.620 --> 16:49.770
Thank you so much!

16:50.130 --> 16:52.280
Sorry I had to duck out like that...

16:52.770 --> 16:55.330
There was an urgent data correction 
I had to take care of.

16:55.330 --> 16:56.530
Shinozaki-san?!

16:57.670 --> 16:58.780
Then, who's...

17:01.340 --> 17:03.390
This Meowtaro?

17:06.730 --> 17:07.670
It's me!

17:07.670 --> 17:09.420
Wha—

17:10.420 --> 17:12.770
Go and give her a big hug!

17:13.180 --> 17:14.670
Cut it out!

17:14.670 --> 17:18.740
Come on, they're announcing the winner! 
Let's get back to the hall!

17:18.740 --> 17:21.200
No hug, then?

17:21.200 --> 17:23.180
Stop, Manager!

17:23.180 --> 17:29.810
<b>Results Announcement</b>

17:24.420 --> 17:29.810
The time has come. I will now be announcing 
the results of the new hire competition.

17:30.340 --> 17:32.630
Who the heck is gonna win?

17:33.410 --> 17:36.180
That Meowtaro was Akina-san?

17:34.150 --> 17:35.290
Hey there!

17:36.180 --> 17:40.190
Now, before the prizes are presented, 
a few words from the president.

17:41.330 --> 17:44.330
<b>Most Valuable New Hire Award</b>

17:41.650 --> 17:44.670
Before we announce 
the most valuable rookie award,

17:44.330 --> 17:47.830
<b>Excellence Award Team 1</b>

17:44.330 --> 17:47.830
<b>Excellence Award Team 2</b>

17:45.100 --> 17:47.830
I'd like to award the two teams 
receiving the awards for excellence.

17:48.300 --> 17:50.340
The first will be going to...

17:50.710 --> 17:53.490
Shinozaki's team with Development Group 2!

17:54.010 --> 17:55.590
The other...

17:56.190 --> 17:58.840
Kurusu's team with Development Group 1!

17:58.840 --> 18:02.850
<b><b>Most Valuable New Hire Award</b></b>

17:58.840 --> 18:02.850
<b>Excellence Award
Development Group 2
Team Shinozaki</b>

17:58.840 --> 18:02.850
<b>Excellence Award
Development Group 1
Team Kurusu</b>

17:59.430 --> 18:02.850
These are our excellence 
award winners! Congratulations!

18:02.850 --> 18:06.480
I guess I ended up tying with Kurusu-san.

18:07.050 --> 18:08.750
The Okinawan resort...

18:10.170 --> 18:12.020
What are you talking about?

18:12.020 --> 18:14.120
You might not have won 
the most promising rookie,

18:14.120 --> 18:16.240
but the excellence award is great, too!

18:16.940 --> 18:18.360
You should be happy!

18:20.100 --> 18:21.510
You're right!

18:22.790 --> 18:24.570
An award of excellence, eh?

18:26.380 --> 18:29.120
I'm so sorry...

18:29.660 --> 18:31.580
Whatever for?

18:31.580 --> 18:37.990
Everyone helped me... but I 
couldn't win most valuable new hire...

18:40.130 --> 18:42.640
No one's upset with you for that.

18:43.890 --> 18:47.280
Congratulations on your award, Kurusu.

18:48.540 --> 18:51.600
But you won't get their manager now...

18:51.920 --> 18:54.890
You said you needed him for your ambitions...

18:56.780 --> 18:59.620
I was so focused on 
the competition I forgot about that!

18:59.620 --> 19:02.280
You forgot?!

19:02.280 --> 19:02.950
Yeah.

19:03.830 --> 19:04.950
Besides...

19:04.950 --> 19:08.450
<b>You're a-meow-zing,
Dev Group 1 Team Kurusu</b>

19:05.550 --> 19:08.450
Seeing everyone work so hard 
made me realize something.

19:09.260 --> 19:12.210
All I need to strive for greater heights...

19:14.170 --> 19:16.090
are my valuable subordinates.

19:17.150 --> 19:18.340
Director...

19:19.310 --> 19:21.840
Here's to further working together, Kurusu.

19:22.530 --> 19:23.330
Right!

19:26.010 --> 19:29.750
And now, at long last, we will be announcing 
the most valuable rookie award!

19:27.100 --> 19:31.980
<b><b>Most Valuable New Hire Award</b></b>

19:27.100 --> 19:31.980
<b>Excellence Award
Development Group 2
Team Shinozaki</b>

19:27.100 --> 19:31.980
<b>Excellence Award
Development Group 1
Team Kurusu</b>

19:30.160 --> 19:35.480
Out of all the submissions, the one selected 
for the most prestigious prize is...

19:35.890 --> 19:38.480
Yamagishi's team from Public Relations!

19:39.740 --> 19:42.190
No way... Me?

19:42.190 --> 19:44.120
Yay!

19:44.120 --> 19:46.440
Where did you get the idea 
for your proposal from?

19:46.440 --> 19:48.220
Nowhere in particular...

19:48.220 --> 19:51.090
It's all thanks to my daily guidance!

19:51.090 --> 19:54.040
He was the least motivated, and yet...!

19:54.040 --> 19:57.000
This is... really frustrating.

19:57.620 --> 20:01.930
And that concludes the annual 
new hire competition.

20:02.900 --> 20:06.000
Shinozaki-san, you did a great job!

20:06.000 --> 20:08.650
There's a big wrap party to celebrate, too.

20:08.650 --> 20:10.930
It'll be my victory party!

20:10.930 --> 20:11.920
No, it won't be.

20:11.920 --> 20:13.020
Right?!

20:26.350 --> 20:30.230
<i>Bleary-eyed and not fully awake from a dream</i>

20:30.230 --> 20:35.130
<i>I still can't bring myself 
to drink that bitter coffee</i>

20:35.690 --> 20:39.610
<i>So I sneakily toss in 
two pinches of a sweet secret</i>

20:39.610 --> 20:43.830
<i>And let it slowly spread throughout</i>

20:45.050 --> 20:48.790
<i>There's a local bakery 
that's only open sometimes</i>

20:48.790 --> 20:53.680
<i>Where I once had some toast that glittered</i>

20:54.340 --> 20:58.180
<i>What is it that makes it so satisfying?</i>

20:58.180 --> 21:02.350
<i>Almost like magic</i>

21:02.770 --> 21:07.430
<i>I find myself thinking about that kind of thing</i>

21:07.430 --> 21:13.040
<i>How the small things can be the most precious</i>

21:13.790 --> 21:17.830
<i>Deep inside my heart</i>

21:17.830 --> 21:22.230
<i>It's ever so bittersweet</i>

21:23.100 --> 21:27.150
<i>"Just being around you is enough"</i>

21:27.150 --> 21:31.170
<i>Becomes my mantra</i>

21:31.170 --> 21:33.460
<i>Baby like sugar</i>

21:40.570 --> 21:42.720
<i>Baby you're the sugar</i>

21:45.310 --> 21:48.290
Work drags so much in the afternoon...

21:48.290 --> 21:49.560
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

21:49.560 --> 21:51.450
Just the excellence one.

21:51.910 --> 21:55.010
It ain't like that at all!

21:59.080 --> 22:00.210
Holler at you later!

22:02.090 --> 22:04.340
Forget... what you heard.

22:04.340 --> 22:06.090
Not gonna happen that fast.

22:07.090 --> 22:08.720
Don't try the physical approach.

22:09.820 --> 22:11.930
What's the big deal anyway?

22:11.930 --> 22:14.490
It's... embarrassing.

22:14.490 --> 22:16.730
I don't see how.

22:17.270 --> 22:22.750
We don't have any sort of obvious accent 
where I'm from, so I'm kinda jealous.

22:24.270 --> 22:25.990
Jealous...?

22:26.280 --> 22:27.990
Yeah, it's kinda cool.

22:30.240 --> 22:33.120
Man, lunch is gonna end 
if we don't wrap up here.

22:33.120 --> 22:34.740
H-Hey...

22:37.610 --> 22:39.250
Thank you kindly.

22:42.290 --> 22:43.770
Thank me whatly?
